housands of  terrified Christians fled escaping to  Christian towns in this region until  Isis got so close they evacuated from  here too at one point the terrorist  group was just a 10-minute Drive away  from the Christian town of al-kahf that  sits at the base of the mountain  mercifully they never made it any closer  but the threat is still felt today here  praying to your God means planning for  the worst that armed bodyguard follows  the priests everywhere such a something  the monasteries head monk father den ha  Toma knows all too well he was in the  nearby city of Mosul  when Isis suddenly invaded five years  ago what do you think Isis would have  done if they reached this place when  Michael Sonny wherever they saw a cross  they smashed it he said I thought it  would be erased any traces of  Christianity huh da man even the Virgin  Mary there used to be a statue of her  they chopped the head off and left the  rest of the statue standing there if  they had reached here he said they would  have certainly destroyed this monastery  [Applause]  before the us-led invasion the  insurgency and Isis around one and a  half million Christians in Iraq there  are now barely 250,000 in fact there are  now more Chaldean Catholics the most  followed denomination among Iraqi  Christians in the United States than in  Iraq  [Music]  the regional archbishop recently  described Christianity in Iraq is being  perilously close to extinction which  means one of the oldest continuous  Christian communities in existence now  remains on a cliff edge for CBS this  morning Charlie d'Agata al kasha  northern Iraq
 

